{
  "id": "00030_chikau",
  "headword": "{誓|ちか}う",
  "reading": "ちかう",
  "part_of_speech": "godan verb",
  "gloss": "to swear; to vow; to pledge",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "godan",
    "ending": "う",
    "stem": "{誓|ちか}"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to swear; to vow; to take an oath",
      "explanation": "To make a solemn promise or declaration, often with religious or formal significance."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to pledge; to promise solemnly",
      "explanation": "To commit oneself firmly to a course of action or to another person."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "00030_chikau_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{永遠|えいえん}→永遠：01873_eien⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{愛|あい}→愛：02370_ai⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{誓|ちか}う。",
      "english": "To vow eternal love.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "00030_chikau_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{二度|にど}→二度：09503_nido⟧⟦と→と：00512_to⟧⟦{嘘|うそ}→嘘：01796_uso⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦つかない→つく：01960_tsuku⟧⟦と→と：00512_to⟧{誓|ちか}った。",
      "english": "I swore never to lie again.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "00030_chikau_ex3",
      "japanese": "⟦{神|かみ}→神：02147_kami⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{誓|ちか}って、⟦{私|わたし}→私：02988_watashi⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧⟦{無実|むじつ}→無実：09504_mujitsu⟧⟦です→です：09485_desu⟧。",
      "english": "I swear to God, I am innocent.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "00030_chikau_ex4",
      "japanese": "{選手|せんしゅ}たちは{開会式|かいかいしき}で{正々堂々|せいせいどうどう}と{戦|たたか}うことを{誓|ちか}った。",
      "english": "The athletes vowed at the opening ceremony to compete fairly.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "00030_chikau_ex5",
      "japanese": "もう{二度|にど}と{同|おな}じ{失敗|しっぱい}はしないと{自分|じぶん}に{誓|ちか}った。",
      "english": "I pledged to myself that I would never make the same mistake again.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{誓|ちか}う is transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). It takes the object marker を for what is being sworn.\n\nASPECT ({ている}):\n{誓|ちか}っている indicates an ongoing state of having made a vow, or the act of swearing in progress.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {愛|あい}を{誓|ちか}う (to vow love)\n- {忠誠|ちゅうせい}を{誓|ちか}う (to pledge allegiance)\n- {神|かみ}に{誓|ちか}う (to swear to God)\n- ～することを{誓|ちか}う (to vow to do ~)\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- ～を{誓|ちか}う: What is being sworn\n- ～に{誓|ちか}う: To whom/what one swears\n\nRegister: Neutral to formal. Used in serious contexts such as ceremonies, courts, and solemn promises.",
